<report>
<title>Sample size for independent case-control study</title>

<p>Probability of exposure in controls = @{pc:roundu}<br />
Probability of exposure in cases = @{ps:roundu}<br />
Controls per case subject = @cpc<br />
Alpha = @{alpha:roundu}<br />
Power = @{power:roundu}</p>

<p>For uncorrected chi-square test:<br />
N = @case case subjects and @controls controls</p>

<p><b>For corrected chi-square and Fisher's exact tests:</b><br />
N = @case_corr case subjects and @controls_corr controls</p>
<block name="assumptions">

<p><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.</warn><br />
<warn>However, true power associated with @cases cases will be no less than @no_less and no greater than @no_greater.</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
